# The owner's ruling of 2026-11-21 (docs/engine-design.md, "Taking back an illegal action"): a part of a cost that would make
# hidden information known is chosen as it is paid and carried out only as the spell is committed, so a cast given up shows
# nothing. Force of Will's alternative cost is 1 life and a blue card exiled from the hand (CR 118.9); Silverquill, the
# Disputant gives it casualty 1 (CR 702.153a), whose sacrifice is chosen after the exile (CR 601.2h), so there is a question
# to give the cast up at once the blue card is chosen. Bot1 casts Memnite and, holding priority, Force of Will at it.
# The first time Brainstorm is chosen and the cast is given up at the casualty's question: Brainstorm never left the hand -
# nothing is in exile while the cast is under way - and the take-back leaves Bot1 on 20 with Force of Will in hand (CR 733.1).
# The second time the cast is completed: the Elves are sacrificed and, as the cast is committed, Brainstorm is exiled and the
# 1 life paid. Casualty's copy counters Memnite and Force of Will, its target gone, does nothing.

